From 3c134587209e59bf9990cd20d76f2213e50b4384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 04:44:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(slideshow): move arrows outside card, add
 drag-to-swipe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Refinements to the featured-work slideshow on the homepage — all
additive; autoplay, arrow navigation, keyboard nav, dots and pause-on-
hover keep working exactly as before.

Arrows outside the card:
- On wide screens (>= lg) the prev/next arrow buttons now sit in the
  outer gutters beside the card rather than overlaying the cover image.
  The card gets a cleaner look and the arrows are easier to reach.
- On narrower desktop widths (sm–lg) there isn't room in the gutters,
  so the arrows render below the card flanking the dot indicators.
  Dots-only layout on >= lg; arrows + dots together on < lg.

Drag-to-swipe:
- New motion.div drag layer wraps the AnimatePresence so the drag
  handle survives slide re-keying.
- drag="x" with dragConstraints locked to 0 (elastic pull, no free
  pan) and dragElastic 0.18 for a subtle rubber-band feel.
- Swipe commit thresholds: 80 px of offset OR 500 px/s of velocity,
  whichever is reached first — matches native carousel feel.
- Drag pauses autoplay; autoplay resumes ~200ms after release.
- Click guard on the slide link via isDraggingRef so ending a swipe
  doesn't accidentally navigate into the case-study page.
- touch-pan-y preserves native vertical scroll on mobile-sized
  viewports (the slideshow is hidden on < sm anyway, but safe for
  tablet widths).

No behavior change to the mobile layout (still up to 3 stacked cards +
'ver todos' button to /work).
