From 65fa837011afcbf35abd06e1091ca82f4b7a743e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 04:44:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(preloader): revert intro audio integration, play
 sound after exit

Splits the audio out of the preloader and moves it to a dedicated
post-preloader player. The preloader is back to its original behavior
(pure typewriter + fixed settle); the sound now fires the moment the
preloader finishes and the main content becomes visible.

components/Preloader.tsx:
- Reverted to the pre-audio version (byte-identical to main before
  PR #2). No audio element, no async play() attempt, no audio-ended
  dismissal path, no 6s safety timeout.

components/PostPreloaderSound.tsx (new):
- Small client component with a hidden <audio> element.
- Takes a 'trigger' boolean prop; when it flips true, attempts to play
  the source exactly once. A ref guards against double-play on
  re-renders.
- Autoplay rejections are swallowed silently so the rest of the page
  is never affected (browsers generally block programmatic audio
  without a prior user gesture).
- Respects prefers-reduced-motion: skips the sound entirely.

app/page.tsx:
- Mounts <PostPreloaderSound trigger={preloaderDone} /> alongside the
  preloader. The preloader's onDone callback (fired from
  onExitComplete) flips preloaderDone, which is exactly the moment we
  want the sound to play.

public/audio/:
- Removes the old eterlab-intro.mp3 (3.5s, used by the reverted
  preloader integration).
- Adds eterlab-intro-song.mp3 (0.47s, the new post-preloader sound).
